      sayZh: '在患难之日胆怯，力量就微小（24:10）；人被拉到死地，你要解救，将被杀的，你须拦阻（24:11）；不可用“我未曾知道”推卸，因那衡量人心的神都明白（24:12）。',
      sayEn: 'If you falter in the day of trouble, your strength is small (24:10); rescue those being led away to death; hold back those staggering to slaughter (24:11); don’t excuse yourself with “I didn’t know,” for the God who weighs hearts understands (24:12).',
      meanZh: '这一段有两层信息。一是关于我们自己：患难是检验力量的时刻，真正的力量在压力下才显出来。二是关于我们对别人的责任：当看见有人正走向毁灭，袖手旁观、假装不知道，在神眼中并不是无辜。智慧不只顾自己站稳，也伸手拉住别人。',
      meanEn: 'This cluster carries two messages. One is about ourselves: trouble is the test of strength, and real strength shows only under pressure. The other is about our responsibility to others: when we see someone heading toward destruction, standing by and pretending not to know is not innocence in God’s eyes. Wisdom not only stands firm itself but reaches out to hold on to others.',
      forMeZh: '此刻有没有一处，我看见有人正陷入危险或毁灭，却用“这不关我事”“我不确定”来让自己心安？神看得见我真实的心。',
      forMeEn: 'Is there a place right now where I see someone sliding toward danger or ruin, and I quiet myself with “not my business” or “I’m not sure”? God sees my real heart.',
