      sayEn: 'A righteous person falls seven times and rises again, but the wicked are overthrown by calamity (24:16). Don’t rejoice when your enemy falls; don’t let your heart be glad when he is overthrown (24:17–18).',
      meanZh: '“义人”的标志，不是从不跌倒，而是跌倒后总会靠着神再起来。这对每一个在失败中灰心的人，是极大的安慰——你的跌倒不是定论。紧接着的劝勉同样深刻：即使是对仇敌，也不可幸灾乐祸，因为那种暗自的快意，会腐蚀我们自己的心。',
      meanEn: 'The mark of a “righteous person” is not never falling but always getting up again by God’s help. To anyone discouraged by failure, this is enormous comfort — your fall is not the final word. The charge that follows is just as searching: even toward an enemy, don’t gloat, because that secret satisfaction corrodes our own heart.',
      forMeZh: '我是不是把一次失败当成了“我这个人就这样了”？神说的是：起来。同时，我心里有没有对某个人跌倒的暗暗快意，需要在神面前处理？',
      forMeEn: 'Have I taken one failure as “this is just who I am”? God says: get up. And is there a secret satisfaction over someone’s downfall in my heart that I need to bring before God?',
